1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,580
So if you're holding one tonight, here's the only thing I ask

2
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:08,260
Don't leave it in a drawer to gather dust with all your past

3
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:12,020
Find a pencil, find a neighbor, find a window with no light

4
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:16,260
Write the words you wish somebody would have told you on your night

5
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:19,540
Leave it on a windshield, tuck it in a library book

6
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:23,460
Slip it in a stranger's pocket when nobody's there to look

7
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:27,060
It doesn't have to be pretty, and it doesn't have to rhyme

8
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:30,820
Just light one, let it go, one window at a time

9
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:32,740
Then one night I'm at the window

10
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:34,500
And I see a little glow

11
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,500
Coming back across the rooftops

12
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:38,500
From a stranger I don't know

13
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,260
Then another, then a hundred

14
00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:42,260
Till the whole sky caught the flame

15
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:44,260
Every light I ever sent you

16
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:47,060
You were sending back again

17
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:49,060
I don't know how many mornings

18
00:00:49,060 --> 00:00:50,980
Are still written in my name

19
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:53,780
But I know the light keeps traveling

20
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:57,540
Long after the flame
